# valgrind suppressions for `bash run-tests.sh valgrind`.
#
# Only Z3-internal frames belong here, each with a sourced reason. A
# suppression must never cover a frame in src/z3: a wrapper defect has to
# fail the gate.

# UPS-03: an invalid read of size 1 in spacer::pob_queue::reset(), inside
# libz3, on a second Z3_fixedpoint_query against the same Spacer
# fixedpoint. The block was freed earlier in the same
# spacer::context::solve_core; no nim-z3 hook is on the alloc or free stack.
# Reduced to a 4-line input and filed as Z3Prover/z3#11601 (reproduces on
# 4.13.4, 5.1.0 and the 2026-11-07 master nightly; fixed upstream by
# b2daca7f). See docs/GOTCHAS.md section 25. libz3 5.1 ships stripped, so
# the read is matched by object, size and the exported entry point.
{
   ups03-spacer-pob-queue-reset
   Memcheck:Addr1
   obj:*libz3.so*
   ...
   fun:Z3_fixedpoint_query
}
